  "scope_notes": "Extracts BlockAssembler::CreateCoinbaseTx() from BlockAssembler::CreateNewBlock() as a non-behavior-changing refactor to share coinbase construction between internal template generation and TxCollection dummy-coinbase validation.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Adds a TxCollection mining IPC interface allowing external services like Stratum v2 Job Declarator Servers (JDS) to assemble and validate candidate block templates from a list of witness transaction IDs using the local node's mempool. External template validators currently have to maintain a separate out-of-process mirror mempool and poll full templates or missing transactions, duplicating state and wasting bandwidth. The new interface identifies which transactions are missing, ingests them from the client, and validates the resulting block template against the chain tip using TestBlockValidity. Demonstrated against the Stratum v2 reference implementation in sv2-apps PR 599.",
